</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Mobile Placement Hard</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the Mobile Placement Hard benchmark, we construct a long-table environment with chairs positioned around the perimeter and varied objects distributed on the table surface.
The robot is required to identify approachable regions unobstructed by chairs or densely placed tabletop items.
The table periphery is systematically divided into <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math> candidate zones (three per long side, one per short side, and four corners), each classified as either occupied (by chairs or dense objects, excluding corners) or vacant (clear spaces or sparse-object areas permitting approach).
We additionally distribute random objects in the central table area, which improves visual realism and increases scene diversity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each simulation scenario involves randomized assignment of occupancy states to candidate regions, with objects sampled from a <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>70</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">70</annotation></semantics></math>-category office inventory (e.g., monitors, books, mugs).
The robot is initialized <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math> meters from the table edge (<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 15\deg" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>deg</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 15\deg</annotation></semantics></math> angular deviation) to observe the table and surroundings.
The evaluation requires the model to predict feasible placement points, followed by robot execution attempts.
Performance is assessed in <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> simulated scenarios, where we measure the success rates of planning placement trajectories.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS2.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="815.81" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 815.81" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,815.81) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 809.91 C 0 813.17 2.64 815.81 5.91 815.81 L 544.09 815.81 C 547.36 815.81 550 813.17 550 809.91 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FCFCFF;" fill="#FCFCFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 809.91 C 1.97 812.08 3.73 813.85 5.91 813.85 L 544.09 813.85 C 546.27 813.85 548.03 812.08 548.03 809.91 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 404.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:28.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:28.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="788.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 397.59)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
